              <p>Yes in every practical sense. Kindle+ is the new name for the same Amazon subscription that was previously called Kindle Unlimited. The lending rules, the price, the device support, and the 20-borrow limit are unchanged. The differences are the branding, the rewritten marketing copy, and the addition of audiobooks to the catalog for US subscribers. Existing Kindle Unlimited memberships carried over into Kindle+ automatically.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div itemscope itemprop="mainEntity" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question">
